  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "gVA54JtTRCVntYuU8mqFXRVznIw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:39:27.716Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "v6.0.0 lists the rename under Breaking Changes with no migration table:\n\n> **`DriveEditor` renamed** \u2014 a bulk rename was applied across all packages. Search your codebase for old `DriveEditor` references and update as directed by TypeScript.\n\nThe intended workflow is therefore compile-error-driven rather than documented symbol-by-symbol, which is worth knowing before going looking for a mapping that does not exist.\n\nThe terminology landed on **Drive-app**, and the concept is now a first-class generated module type rather than a special kind of editor. The CLI reference confirms the surface:\n\n- `ph generate app` \u2014 \"Generate a drive app\", with `--name`, `--document-types`, `--dir`, `--all`, `--extract`, and a `--disable-drag-and-drop` flag.\n- Its spec files are `powerhouse/app` documents: `--document` takes \"Path to a `powerhouse/app` spec file (.phd or .json) to drive codegen\", and `--extract` writes \"a `powerhouse/app` spec for each existing drive app into `specs/apps/`\".\n- The CSS customization reference maps the `app-editor` slot to document type `powerhouse/app`.\n\nSo the rename is not only cosmetic: it aligns the drive-level UI with the same spec-document-as-source-of-truth model used for document models and editors, each with its own document type and its own `ph generate` subcommand.\n\nThe other subgraph-shaped breaking change in the same release reinforces the direction \u2014 generated subgraph code should be **deleted** (`rm -rf src/subgraphs/`) because subgraphs are now generated and loaded at runtime.\n\nProvenance: academy `ReleaseNotes/v6.0.0.md:192` (Breaking Changes) for the rename; `04-Reference/07-CLITooling/00-PowerhouseCLI.md` App section and `03-Build/03-BuildingUserExperiences/04-CSSCustomization.md:135` for the `powerhouse/app` type and `ph generate app`. Academy 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:39:26.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:39:27.716Z"
    }
  },
